  "generated_text": "To expand the product \\((x^2-2x+2)(x^2+2x+2)\\), we use the distributive property of multiplication over addition. Let's do this step by step:\n\n\\[\n(x^2-2x+2)(x^2+2x+2) = x^2(x^2+2x+2) - 2x(x^2+2x+2) + 2(x^2+2x+2)\n\\]\n\nNow, we expand each term:\n\n\\[\nx^2(x^2+2x+2) = x^4 + 2x^3 + 2x^2\n\\]\n\\[\n-2x(x^2+2x+2) = -2x^3 - 4x^2 - 4x\n\\]\n\\[\n2(x^2+2x+2) = 2x^2 + 4x + 4\n\\]\n\nAdding all these terms together:\n\n\\[\nx^4 + 2x^2 + 4\n\\]\n\nThus, the expanded form of the product is \\(\\boxed{x^4 + 2x^2 + 4}\\).",
